1. Created a mock implementation of the next/font/google module
2. Added the mock to the global window object to handle potential imports
3. Switched to a useEffect-based component loading approach
4. Simplified the component structure and error handling
5. Added better error logging
6. Removed the React.lazy implementation in favor of manual module loading
7. Added proper type safety and error boundaries
8. Separated loading and error states into distinct components

The main changes focus on:
- Mocking the next/font/google module at the window level
- Using a simpler component loading strategy
- Providing better error handling and logging
- Making the component more resilient to loading failures

This approach should handle the font module error by providing a mock implementation before the component tries to access it. The component will now:
1. Load with proper error handling
2. Have access to the mocked font module
3. Fallback gracefully if there are any issues

